Z||000000||NIFE [PaulV]||11-08-2001||03:29 PM||||About once a year I try to update the National Fiero club list I maintain on<BR>my web site. While I update it regularly with input from various messages<BR>and forums, I know that there are  changes and additions that I don't hear<BR>about.<BR>To be listed, a club needs to provide a club name, club contact (usually the<BR>president), mailing address, phone #, and  email/web site if available.<BR>I would appreciate if current club members can check their listing on the<BR>web site shown below, and advise of any changes. Clubs are listed by state<BR>on the site.<BR>I am missing the following:<BR>Phone # for Fieros West<BR>Phone # for  Tampa Fiero Club<BR>Phone # for Jet City Fieros<BR>Several clubs do not show any email for the contact individual.<P>This list is used for publication in FOCOA magazine, and for anyone looking<BR>for a club to participate in. I would appreciate anyone that has a Fiero web<BR>site to include the URL as a link on their page. Also, if any vendor or club<BR>would like the club list in excel format to run a mailing label merge, I can<BR>provide it. Our club mails a complimentary NIFE Fiero Focus 16 page<BR>bi-monthly newsletter to any club who sends us their newsletter.<BR>Thanks, Club list as follows<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/national.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/national.htm</A> <P>Paul Vargyas<BR>Northern Illinois Fiero Enthusiasts<BR>Lisle, IL. (Chicago area)<BR>Web site  <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~paulv" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~paulv</A> <BR>||||reg||1
